From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 14:09:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebPlayer: let the red button of an HbbTV web app hide it or
 not

On a television the red button hides an HbbTV application to show the
broadcast behind it. Kodi has no broadcast behind a web app, so apps
such as ORF ON and ARD Mediathek leave an empty screen on red; whether
red hides them is chosen by a query parameter of their start URL.

kodi.webapp 1.4.0 adds the manifest element <redbutton on="..."
off="..."/>, naming the query parameter for red hiding the app and for
red staying inside it. An app that has it gets the setting "Red button
hides the app to show the TV picture", off by default, and RunAddon
appends the parameter of the chosen state to the start URL. A URL
handed to RunAddon is opened as given.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
